            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="1337" n="1179" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1179"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of the Netherlands to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Royal Legation of the Netherlands</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-03-30"><hi rendition="#italic">March 30,
                        1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 173.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: By order of my
                    Government I have the honor to request your excellency to inform me whether,
                    according to the laws in force on the subject in the United States, the person
                    named H. R. J. C. Van Hall is considered by the American Government as still
                    possessing American nationality.</p>
                <p>As your excellency will gather from the accompanying documents, Van Hall was born
                    on July 16, 1887, and baptized on September 17 following at Helena, Mont. His
                    father, Henry Van Hall, a Hollander by birth, had become an American citizen in
                    1876.</p>
                <p>The father left the United States on September 26, 1891, and has since resided
                    with his family at Ravenstein, Netherlands.</p>
                <pb facs="1338" n="1180" xml:id="pg1180"/>
                <p>Thanking your excellency in advance for whatever information you may be pleased
                    to give me, and requesting you to kindly return to me the accompanying
                    inclosures after use,</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Van Swinderen.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
